   {
    "context": "1 Peter 3:15. You don't need to abandon the canons of logic, rationality, and truth in order to exemplify these biblical virtues. And as for the idea that people in our culture are no longer interested or responsive to rational argumentation and evidence for Christianity, well, nothing could be farther from the truth. If I might speak from my own experience, for over 20 years I've been engaged in speaking evangelistically on university campuses in North America and Europe.",
    "dist": 0.4164,
    "occurrence_id": 26656,
    "published_at": "2012-01-11T07:19:48Z",
    "role": "host",
    "surface": "truth",
    "t": 1810.6,
    "title": "Christian Apologetics: Who Needs It? - William Lane Craig",
    "video_id": "KDH-_4vkKUk"
   },
   {
    "context": "We know what the truth is. We know there's a God, we know there's a creator God, we know there's a moral God. It's written on our hearts, but we suppress that because we want to do our own thing. You can't know anything for sure. Whenever you're right, you're just borrowing from my worldview. You just want to sin, you're suppressing the truth. These are but a few among the charges of heresy, leveled at every non-believer. But regardless of who's doing it, these tactics serve only to obfuscate, not to illuminate.",
    "dist": 0.4202,
    "occurrence_id": 10274,
    "published_at": "2020-08-28T16:00:03Z",
    "role": "unknown",
    "surface": "truth",
    "t": 1266.28,
    "title": "Christianity's Most Toxic Idea [and Its Ancient Origins]",
    "video_id": "78NQtotfdJI"
   },
   {
    "context": "If your entire fate, heaven and hell hinges on a doctrine that no one can explain without contradiction and dishonesty, maybe you're actually in the right for doubting, deconstructing, or deconverting and rejecting it. Maybe you're the one who actually cares about truth more than the religion that claims their God is the definition of truth. Because if this God really wanted to reveal himself, if he really wanted to leave behind his spirit to guide us and empower us, to give us knowledge, wisdom, and discernment, it wouldn't look like this.",
